  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "This report investigates how knowledge entanglement in large language models (LLMs) predicts whether unlearned facts can leak after unlearning, and how unlearning impacts both private and public information. It evaluates different unlearning algorithms and their effectiveness across various models and domains.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The study finds that more entangled facts are recalled more often during unlearning, with a positive correlation (r = +0.39–0.51).",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Unlearning algorithms like WHP and GA+KL show different effects: WHP weakens the relationship but remains positive, while GA+KL inverts it in all domains and models.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The study proposes a predictive model to estimate a prompt's post-unlearning factuality/hallucination profile before unlearning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
